NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000018 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000019 "=head1 NAME"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000020 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000021 "Sah::Schemas::JSON - Various schemas related to JSON"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000022 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000023 "=head1 VERSION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000024 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000025 "This document describes version 0.007 of Sah::Schemas::JSON (from Perl distribution Sah-Schemas-JSON), released on 2022-11-15."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000026 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000027 "=head1 SAH SCHEMAS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000028 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000029 "The following schemas are included in this distribution:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000030 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000031 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000032 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000033 "=item * L<any_from_json|Sah::Schema::any_from_json>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000034 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000035 "A data structure, coerced from JSON string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000036 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000037 "You can use this schema if you want to accept any data (a data structure or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000038 "simple scalar), but if user supplies a defined string e.g. in a command-line"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000039 "script as command-line argument or option, the string will be assumed to be a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000040 "JSON-encoded value and decoded. Data will not be valid if the string does not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000041 "contain valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000042 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000043 "Thus, if you want to supply a string, you have to JSON-encode it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000044 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000045 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000046 "=item * L<array_from_json|Sah::Schema::array_from_json>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000047 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000048 "Array, coercible from JSON string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000049 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000050 "You can use this schema if you want to accept an array, but if user supplies a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000051 "string e.g. in a command-line script as command-line argument or option, the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000052 "string will be coerced into array if the string contains a JSON-encoded array."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000053 "Data will not be valid if the string does not contain valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000054 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000055 "Note that array data is accepted, unlike the C<json_str::array> schema which only"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000056 "accepts JSON-encoded array in string form."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000057 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000058 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000059 "=item * L<hash_from_json|Sah::Schema::hash_from_json>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000060 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000061 "Hash, coerced from JSON string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000062 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000063 "You can use this schema if you want to accept a hash, but if user supplies a"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000064 "string e.g. in a command-line script as command-line argument or option, the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000065 "string will be coerced into hash if the string contains a JSON-encoded object"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000066 "(hash). Data will not be valid if the string does not contain valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000067 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000068 "Note that hash data is accepted, unlike the C<json_str::hash> schema which only"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000069 "accepts hash in JSON-encoded string form."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000070 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000071 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000072 "=item * L<json_or_str|Sah::Schema::json_or_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000073 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000074 "A JSON-encoded data or string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000075 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000076 "You can use this schema if you want to accept any data (a data structure or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000077 "simple scalar), and if user supplies a defined string e.g. in a command-line"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000078 "script as command-line argument or option, it will be tried to be JSON-decoded"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000079 "first. If the string does not contain valid JSON, it will be left as-is as"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000080 "string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000081 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000082 "This schema is convenient on the command-line where you want to accept data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000083 "structure via command-line argument or option. But you have to be careful when"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000084 "you want to pass a string like C<null>, C<true>, C<false>; you have to quote it to"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000085 "C<\"null\">, C<\"true\">, C<\"false\"> to prevent it being decoded into undef or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000086 "boolean values."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000087 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000088 "See also related schema: C<json_str>, C<str::encoded_json>, C<str::escaped_json>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000089 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000090 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000091 "=item * L<json_str|Sah::Schema::json_str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000092 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000093 "A string that contains valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000094 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000095 "This schema can be used if you want to accept a string that contains valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000096 "The JSON string will not be decoded (e.g. a JSON-encoded array will not beome an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000097 "array) but you know that the string contains a valid JSON. Data will not be"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000098 "valid if the string does not contain valid JSON."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000099 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000100 "See also related schema: C<json_or_str>, C<str::encoded_json>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000101 "C<str::escaped_json>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000102 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000103 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000104 "=item * L<json_str::array|Sah::Schema::json_str::array>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000105 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000106 "A string that contains valid JSON and the JSON encodes an array."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000107 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000108 "This schema is like the C<json_str> schema: it accepts a string that contains"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000109 "valid JSON. The JSON string will not be decoded but you know that the string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000110 "contains a valid JSON. In addition to that, the JSON must encode an array. Data"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000111 "will not be valid if it is not a valid JSON or if the JSON is not an array."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000112 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000113 "Note that unlike the C<array_from_json> schema, an array data is not accepted by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000114 "this schema. Data must be a string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000115 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000116 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000117 "=item * L<json_str::hash|Sah::Schema::json_str::hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000118 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000119 "A string that contains valid JSON and the JSON encodes a hash (JavaScript object)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000120 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000121 "This schema is like the C<json_str> schema: it accepts a string that contains"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000122 "valid JSON. The JSON string will not be decoded but you know that the string"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000123 "contains a valid JSON. In addition to that, the JSON must encode a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000124 "(JavaScript object). Data will not be valid if it is not a valid JSON or if the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000125 "JSON is not a hash."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000126 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000127 "Note that unlike the C<hash_from_json> schema, a hash data is not accepted by"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000128 "this schema. Data must be a string."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000129 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000130 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000131 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000132 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000133 "=head1 HOMEPAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00000134 ""
